x86_64-linux  Two groups, neither a mangling difference. cxx1 emits `_ZN1BC1Ei`, `_ZN1BD1Ev`, `_ZN1LC1Ei` and `_ZN1MC2Ei`, forms of constructors and destructors nothing here calls - B and L only ever bases, nothing deriving from M - where clang emits only the form it uses. clang's `_Unwind_Resume` and `DW.ref.__gxx_personality_v0` are the cleanup it writes around `new M(5)` to free the memory should the constructor throw, which cxx1 does not write; the same remainder array-static-storage.nonames records. Every name this case is about agrees - `_ZTv0_n32_N1MD1Ev`, `_ZTv0_n32_N1MD0Ev`, `_ZTT1M`, `_ZTC1M0_1L`.
arm64-darwin  The same two groups with Mach-O's leading underscore, less `__ZN1BD1Ev`, which this target's clang emits too.
